1543
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,420
Lady Elianna.

1544
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:19,180
Your schedule for the afternoon has been left open.

1545
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,220
Huh?

1546
00:03:20,470 --> 00:03:23,810
Please take some time to relax, my Lady.

1547
00:03:30,230 --> 00:03:33,730
<i>I've been wanting to go
the Kreis family library for so long!</i>

1548
00:03:34,530 --> 00:03:37,410
My Lady sure is consistent.

1549
00:03:45,040 --> 00:03:46,910
<i>That was interesting.</i>

1550
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:51,920
What should I read next… Hm?

1551
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:55,420
A book about embroidery…

1552
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:58,050
It's badly damaged.

1553
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:04,680
<i>Ladybird Sylvia…</i>

1554
00:04:04,970 --> 00:04:07,310
<i>was this her book?</i>

1555
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:09,560
Don't play games with me.

1556
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:13,400
Both our families would be glad to hear it, right?

1557
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:21,070
Lord Owain, I've told you many times before
that I decline your marriage proposal.

1558
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:28,210
You understand that a maiden of your age
will never have more worth than you do now, yes?

1559
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,170
In year 301 of the Ars Continent calendar,

1560
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:41,010
King Rudolph of the Kingdom of Sauslind, headed eastward
on a military campaign with an enormous army, and failed.

1561
00:04:41,010 --> 00:04:44,310
What do you suppose the reason for that failure was?

1562
00:04:45,010 --> 00:04:45,470
What?

1563
00:04:45,810 --> 00:04:47,640
Again, after that defeat,

1564
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:53,230
the Kingdom of Sauslind was driven to the brink
of total annihilation by a three-country alliance.

1565
00:04:53,810 --> 00:04:58,530
That time, the heroic King Karl
defeated the three-country alliance,

1566
00:04:58,530 --> 00:05:01,740
which lead to the establishment of
the Sauslind Kingdom that we know today.

1567
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:08,750
However, even that heroic king in the height of his rule
permitted many disastrous policies to be passed.

1568
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:12,500
Which one do you think was the prime example of that?

1569
00:05:13,290 --> 00:05:16,050
Eh? What is this sudden spiel?

1570
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:24,470
If you knew these answers, Lord Owain, then you'd realize
just how fruitless your attempts right now are.

1571
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:27,390
Now then, if you will excuse me.

1572
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:28,640
W-Wait!

1573
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:33,150
Lady Elianna?

1574
00:05:37,230 --> 00:05:40,110
Well, this is a coincidence, Lady Elianna.

1575
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:42,910
I am Laennec Owain.

1576
00:05:43,780 --> 00:05:50,370
Being the next crown princess must be suffocating at times.
Whenever you need a breather I will be free to attend to you.

1577
00:05:50,370 --> 00:05:55,670
I appreciate the offer,
but reading is something one does by oneself.

1578
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:05,300
More importantly, Lady Anna, with your permission,
may I attempt to answer your previous questions?

1579
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,680
Yes.

1580
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:12,440
King Rudolph was famous
for having an indiscriminate attraction for women.

1581
00:06:12,890 --> 00:06:15,980
The main reason he failed on his eastern campaign was due to

1582
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:20,940
the power struggles of the members of his harem
who had dragged the local lords into their infighting.

1583
00:06:21,490 --> 00:06:25,410
The supply routes to the troops were cut off as a result.

1584
00:06:25,410 --> 00:06:34,250
The heroic King Karl loved only one consort,
but she died young.

1585
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:41,090
After that, he was attentive to internal disputes,
but paid no mind to the consorts.

1586
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:45,640
As a result, the king was late to notice
how their lavish lifestyles

1587
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:49,680
put considerable financial strain on the country.

1588
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:54,100
There is one lesson to be derived from this:

1589
00:06:54,390 --> 00:07:04,030
Many different rulers have ruined themselves over women,
and have permanently stained history as a result.

1590
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:08,620
That is correct, Lady Elianna.

1591
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,370
Enough of this nonsense!

1592
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:14,870
Are you honestly saying I'd ruin myself over women?!

1593
00:07:15,210 --> 00:07:17,500
Calm down, Lord Laennec.

1594
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:21,670
Silence, you brazen woman!

1595
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:27,430
Powerless females like yourselves
should learn to shut their mouths!

1596
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:32,680
Listen up, my Lady. There's a good method to deal with men
who are behaving like barbarians.

1597
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,060
To take them by surprise...

1598
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:38,560
Make them back away first!

1599
00:07:38,810 --> 00:07:41,570
After that, put all your strength into it.

1600
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:44,940
You need to finish them off in one blow.

1601
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,540
The book!

1602
00:07:57,540 --> 00:07:59,080
What have you done?!

1603
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:02,040
That should be… my line…

1604
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:05,380
Oh no, it's even more damaged…

1605
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:14,600
Lady Anna, are you hurt?

1606
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:16,390
N-No…

1607
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:20,650
Ah yes. It's the son of Baron Owain...

1608
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:24,020
I shall relay this incident in <i>great</i> detail to Chris.

1609
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,620
Eli, are you all right?

1610
00:08:33,990 --> 00:08:36,370
No, I'm not.

1611
00:08:36,370 --> 00:08:40,170
I may have done something terrible…

1612
00:08:41,670 --> 00:08:47,590
It's fine, Lady Elianna.
If we tend to it now, it will still have a long life.

1613
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:49,340
Are you sure?

1614
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:50,300
Yes.

1615
00:08:53,350 --> 00:08:57,140
Lady Elianna, you truly are a book lover, aren't you?

1616
00:08:59,270 --> 00:09:04,190
I wish I could be so openly honest about the things I like.

1617
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:05,270
Huh?

1618
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,410
What's the matter?

1619
00:09:14,030 --> 00:09:15,700
Is everyone all right?!

1620
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:18,540
Lord Theodore! Lord Theodore, I'm so scared!

1621
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:20,080
It was terrifying!

1622
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,040
Lilia?

1623
00:09:21,370 --> 00:09:24,790
We saw it! It was in the old castle!

1624
00:09:24,790 --> 00:09:26,590
The ghost of Eidel!

1625
00:09:26,590 --> 00:09:28,550
The ghost of Eidel?

1626
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:31,800
The daughter of the previous regional lord!

1627
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:33,300
A ghost?

1628
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:35,640
Yes, Lord Theodore!

1629
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:38,810
I've heard that even now
her soul wanders aimlessly, unable to rest!

1630
00:09:39,180 --> 00:09:44,650
They also say that those who catch sight of her
are placed under a horrible curse!

1631
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:49,150
Ladies!

1632
00:09:49,990 --> 00:09:52,110
I heard a scream...

1633
00:09:52,110 --> 00:10:00,450
Ah, everything is fine. Lady Kreis, will you
show the young ladies to somewhere they can rest?

1634
00:10:00,450 --> 00:10:02,290
Yes, of course.

1635
00:10:02,540 --> 00:10:05,290
Ladies, please follow her.

1636
00:10:05,540 --> 00:10:07,500
Are you all doing all right?

1637
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:08,590
Yes.

1638
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:11,050
Lord Theodore.

1639
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:19,970
I'm so frightened! Will you please stay with me
until I can be calm again.

1640
00:10:21,770 --> 00:10:23,190
Lady Sophia.

1641
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:27,520
There's nothing to be afraid of
if you're with everyone else.

1642
00:10:31,030 --> 00:10:33,070
Lady Lilia, watch over the others.

1643
00:10:33,070 --> 00:10:34,950
Okay, will do.

1644
00:10:39,030 --> 00:10:42,960
That was an impressive kick, Lady Elianna.

1645
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:47,840
See you later.

1646
00:10:49,840 --> 00:10:51,210
Lady Elianna.

1647
00:10:52,670 --> 00:10:53,840
Please come with me.

1648
00:10:55,430 --> 00:10:57,140
Lady Anna, would you mind joining us?

1649
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:57,970
Okay.

1650
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:07,440
Now, Lady Elianna.

1651
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:10,690
I am sure I told you not to act alone while you’re here.

1652
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,070
I'm sorry.

1653
00:11:14,110 --> 00:11:17,240
Well, that's how Lady Elianna naturally is.

1654
00:11:17,990 --> 00:11:19,950
Here, have some tea.

1655
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:24,830
Have we met before?

1656
00:11:24,830 --> 00:11:25,580
What?!

1657
00:11:26,210 --> 00:11:29,380
I've been with you
since the start of the hunting festival but...

1658
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:31,090
It's me... Alan.

1659
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,710
I am Alan...

1660
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,710
I am Alan...

1661
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:33,090
Oh! Lord Alan?!

1662
00:11:33,090 --> 00:11:35,340
Do I even exist?

1663
00:11:37,970 --> 00:11:39,090
Lady Elianna.

1664
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:40,970
Lord Sieg.

1665
00:11:40,970 --> 00:11:44,220
I suspect that Prince Christopher knew

1666
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:49,690
some would see your being here
as an opportunity to approach you.

1667
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:55,610
There are people who see you as an easy target
when Chris isn't around.

1668
00:11:56,070 --> 00:11:59,110
While I'm sure it's Alec and his circle that arranged this event,

1669
00:11:59,570 --> 00:12:02,740
there's something off about this year's hunting festival.

1670
00:12:03,450 --> 00:12:05,910
Please act with utmost caution at all times.

1671
00:12:07,330 --> 00:12:09,540
Now, if you'll excuse me.

1672
00:12:19,890 --> 00:12:20,590
Eli.

1673
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:23,390
Do you know the history of the Eidel Domain?

1674
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:30,310
Yes. Before becoming an area
under direct control of the royal family,

1675
00:12:30,310 --> 00:12:34,860
the lord in charge of this land raised a rebellion
against the royal family through Maldura...

1676
00:12:35,150 --> 00:12:39,280
This resulted in the annihilation of his entire house.

1677
00:12:40,030 --> 00:12:44,370
Correct. That particular lord was Duke Slade.

1678
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:48,540
They were in opposition of the royal family of the time.

1679
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:55,130
They joined forces with Maldura, and were seeking an
opportunity to attack the Edea Domain from both sides.

1680
00:12:56,050 --> 00:13:00,630
Then, they had planned to attack
the capital city Saoura after that.

1681
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:04,390
At the time, I was a young boy, not yet ten years old,

1682
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:09,230
but from a political perspective,
my family was considering me for an engagement

1683
00:13:09,230 --> 00:13:11,270
with Duke Slade's fifteen-year-old daughter.

1684
00:13:11,810 --> 00:13:16,150
Is it possible that you met that young lady?

1685
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:23,780
Yes. When I was a child, I was a little sickly.
I've been to the territories for my health before.

1686
00:13:24,580 --> 00:13:26,200
That's where I met her.

1687
00:13:27,330 --> 00:13:29,750
She was somewhat similar to you, Eli.

1688
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:34,840
Then that lady is...

1689
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:38,630
The daughter of the family
who committed the crime of treason.

1690
00:13:38,630 --> 00:13:41,050
I suppose you can guess the end of it.

1691
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:44,680
Goodness...

1692
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:50,180
It's a pain to hear Lord Theodore's
boorish stories of his lady friends, right?

1693
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:53,940
Lady Elianna, I have a message from Prince Christopher.

1694
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:55,190
Oh?

1695
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:01,570
"You should just be yourself, Eli."  That's it.

1696
00:14:03,570 --> 00:14:06,330
That is too sweet for me.

1697
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:10,580
There were actually a lot
of cheesy lines after that, but I kept to the point.

1698
00:14:11,330 --> 00:14:12,830
The prince...

1699
00:14:12,830 --> 00:14:17,340
The fact that I am here
is proof of his feelings for you, my lady.

1700
00:14:20,590 --> 00:14:26,390
<i>How strange... the prince's words have filled me
with a strength I've not felt for some time now. </i><i></i>

1701
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:30,350
<i>Even when he's not with me,</i>

1702
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:33,940
<i>His Highness warms my heart.</i>

1703
00:14:35,310 --> 00:14:40,110
<i>May His Highness also be in good health.</i>

1704
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:46,070
You bandits are fools!

1705
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:49,370
Show no mercy! Cut them down!

1706
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:05,510
Somehow people who are in a particular hurry
always encounter senseless delays like this.

1707
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:07,760
What happened to your Shadows?

1708
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:10,140
The scouting team was assigned to guard Eli.

1709
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,100
What?!

1710
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:12,100
Let's go.

1711
00:15:12,100 --> 00:15:15,140
Whoa, Chris... Wait!

1712
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:18,020
I'm in a hurry!

1713
00:15:18,270 --> 00:15:21,650
We are all acutely aware of that!

1714
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:25,240
First, we deal with the bandits.

1715
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:28,280
After that, you need to take a breather.

1716
00:15:28,570 --> 00:15:31,200
I need nothing but Eli!

1717
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,290
Chris!

1718
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:35,370
Just calm down for now.

1719
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:39,880
If you split your Shadows up to protect her,
then she won't be in that much danger.

1720
00:15:45,510 --> 00:15:52,180
Thank you for subduing the bandits.
Please, stay here tonight.

1721
00:15:52,850 --> 00:15:55,140
I've also prepared the bath for you.

1722
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,100
Thanks.

1723
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:14,950
<i>When running my mind is blank, but now nothing
but bad thoughts are running through my mind.</i>

1724
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:21,460
<i>If anything happens to her, it will be my fault.</i>

1725
00:16:22,420 --> 00:16:25,460
<i>I wanted her by my side...</i>

1726
00:16:26,590 --> 00:16:29,220
<i>If she hadn't become the fiancée of a crown prince, </i><i></i>

1727
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:34,720
<i>she would have lived a peaceful life
surrounded by her beloved books.</i>

1728
00:16:35,850 --> 00:16:39,480
<i>But... I want to keep her by my side!</i>

1729
00:16:40,350 --> 00:16:43,650
<i>I just can't let her go.</i>

1730
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:52,490
I am selfish and self-serving to no end.

1731
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,010
Why?!

1732
00:17:09,470 --> 00:17:13,220
Lord Theodore once again
gives attention to that girl and not me!

1733
00:17:14,390 --> 00:17:15,600
Lady Sophia.

1734
00:17:17,430 --> 00:17:19,980
I have a good idea.

1735
00:17:24,730 --> 00:17:26,730
Beautiful weather today, right, Jean?

1736
00:17:26,730 --> 00:17:31,490
My Lady, quit spacing out and staring up at the sky.
Watch what’s in front of you, please.

1737
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:36,700
Maybe you shouldn't have listened
to what Lady Sophia said.

1738
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:37,870
But...

1739
00:17:38,450 --> 00:17:41,460
If you really are here on Prince Christopher’s behalf

1740
00:17:41,460 --> 00:17:46,750
shouldn't you be commending
the abilities of the men as you watch them?

1741
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:49,840
I think she may be right.

1742
00:17:50,470 --> 00:17:51,800
Lady Elianna!

1743
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,010
Lady Anna!

1744
00:17:56,850 --> 00:17:58,600
<i>She's so gallant!</i>

1745
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:00,850
Please, have one.

1746
00:18:03,230 --> 00:18:04,600
An acorn?

1747
00:18:05,020 --> 00:18:08,980
It looks like the forests of Eidel
had another year of abundance.

1748
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:10,740
That's good.

1749
00:18:11,150 --> 00:18:15,990
I hear the flesh of beasts that eat acorns, nuts, and the like
smell less gamey and taste better.

1750
00:18:16,330 --> 00:18:21,410
Fleshmeats? What an unsettling conversation topic
between a pair of noblewomen.

1751
00:18:27,630 --> 00:18:30,670
That's Lady Sophia's friend...

1752
00:18:30,670 --> 00:18:32,630
Ugh, it's that horse.

1753
00:18:33,010 --> 00:18:36,640
I told them that horse is excitable today
so try not to ride it.

1754
00:18:36,970 --> 00:18:41,640
Actually, that was the horse prepared
for you to ride at first, M'Lady.

1755
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:42,890
Huh?

1756
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:45,060
H-Help me!

1757
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,690
Jean, can't you do something?

1758
00:18:47,690 --> 00:18:52,190
I thought you'd say that. My Lady, please stay put.

1759
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:58,700
I hope she'll be okay.

1760
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:09,630
What a relief. She seems fine.

1761
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:13,130
A wild boar?!

1762
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,390
My Lady!

1763
00:19:17,390 --> 00:19:18,550
Lady Elianna!

1764
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:28,310
<i>Ow... but I'm not in pain...</i>

1765
00:19:30,110 --> 00:19:31,940
<i>Lord Irvin!</i>

1766
00:19:31,940 --> 00:19:32,860
Are you hurt?

1767
00:19:33,530 --> 00:19:36,360
<i>I was saved by Lord Irvin?!</i>

1768
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:39,490
I-I'm all right.

1769
00:19:42,370 --> 00:19:44,410
Is this your arrow?

1770
00:19:45,460 --> 00:19:46,160
No.

1771
00:19:48,920 --> 00:19:50,170
I see.

1772
00:19:50,630 --> 00:19:55,130
Was that wild boar the prey you all have been chasing?

1773
00:19:56,090 --> 00:19:59,800
We do not misdirect our prey.

1774
00:20:00,970 --> 00:20:02,260
Lady Elianna.

1775
00:20:02,890 --> 00:20:06,890
If you are not accustomed to horseback riding,
you may get injured.

1776
00:20:06,890 --> 00:20:11,570
Isn't understanding your own capabilities
another important role of yours?

1777
00:20:11,570 --> 00:20:17,030
Yes... I'm sorry for the trouble I've caused, Count Hayden.

1778
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:19,910
I will search for the one who shot this arrow.

1779
00:20:20,910 --> 00:20:23,870
<i>I've been reprimanded again.</i>

1780
00:20:23,870 --> 00:20:25,410
Lady Elianna,

1781
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:26,460
your hand...

1782
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:29,040
I will see her on her way.

1783
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:29,670
Huh?!

1784
00:20:42,680 --> 00:20:44,930
That's Lord Irvin. He's so dreamy!

1785
00:20:44,930 --> 00:20:47,930
He really saved Lady Elianna from falling off the horse!

1786
00:20:48,230 --> 00:20:52,360
Even so, the two of them look lovely together!

1787
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:58,400
Oh dear, Lady Elianna, I'm so glad you're not injured!

1788
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:01,910
Thank you for your concern.

1789
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:05,830
However, as the fiancée of Prince Christopher,

1790
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:10,210
I'm not sure about you sharing a horse
with someone other than His Highness.

1791
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:11,670
Indeed!

1792
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:15,170
Lady Elianna!

1793
00:21:20,590 --> 00:21:23,430
Thank you so much for what you did!

1794
00:21:23,430 --> 00:21:24,930
Caroline?

1795
00:21:24,930 --> 00:21:27,390
I'm happy you're safe.

1796
00:21:27,390 --> 00:21:31,350
I was so critical of you, and yet...

1797
00:21:31,350 --> 00:21:31,900
Huh?

1798
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:38,150
I was wrong! You are the perfect person
for the crown prince!

1799
00:21:44,740 --> 00:21:49,410
Why did you do this, Rona?! Caroline is on her side now!

1800
00:21:49,410 --> 00:21:54,130
Please stay calm, Lady Sophia. It's all right.

1801
00:21:54,130 --> 00:21:57,420
Really? Is it really okay?

1802
00:21:57,670 --> 00:22:01,930
Yes. I have it all taken care of.

